Tom went to the park. He liked the park because it was peaceful. The trees swayed in the wind, and the birds chirped. Tom sat on a bench and watched the birds. He smiled. 

He had been to the park many times before, but today it felt different. The air was fresh, and the sun was shining brightly. Tom thought about how much he loved this park, and how he always felt happy here.

After a while, Tom stood up and walked around the park. He looked at the flowers, the trees, and the pond. It was all so beautiful.

When it was time to leave, Tom felt calm. He was happy to visit the park again.
